  "aiContextParagraph": "The proposal to appoint three vice presidents was formally initiated by Sultan Najamudin, the Chair of the Regional Representative Council (DPD) of the Republic of Indonesia. According to Najamudin, the concept is designed as a long-term strategic idea rather than an urgent administrative requirement for the current government administration led by President Prabowo Subianto. Proponents of the discussion suggest that the idea should be evaluated comprehensively as part of a broader vision for the nation's governance structure. However, the proposal has encountered varying reactions from the political establishment. For instance, representatives from the NasDem Party have openly questioned the urgency and intended objectives of such a constitutional adjustment. As the government approaches deadlines regarding executive appointments, the debate surrounding the roles and quantity of leadership positions continues to generate discourse among lawmakers and public observers.",
